+2. For each sample $X_i$, evaluate the function value $f(X_i)$ and the probability density $p(X_i)$.
+3. Compute the importance sampling ratio for each sample: $w_i = \frac{f(X_i)}{p(X_i)}$.
+4. Average the ratios to obtain the estimator:
    $$ F_N = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \frac{f(X_i)}{p(X_i)} $$
 
